//! Conception (genetics specification 5.6 and 11.3, ADR-0017 section 4, B18): the woman of
//! a partnership tries once a month from the month after the pairing while she has fewer
//! live births than she wishes, is not pregnant and her fertility has not ended; a
//! successful draw fixes the child at once: its lineage key, the two meioses at the dummy
//! locus and its sex. The pregnancy is state; ten months later the child is born.
//!
//! The expected bytes come from `tools/state_reference.py`, which runs the model of
//! `tools/world_reference.py`, written from the specification and the ADRs and not from
//! this code.
//!
//! Scenario "clan": seed 0xff, founder tag `test:clan`, test data with accident 0.02 per
//! year and the fertility of the old model (ADR-0017 section 5: the woman's window 18 to
//! 45, 0.25 per attempt, ten months, no pause, wish 40). Three founder couples: a woman
//! of 20 and a man of 22; a girl of 12 and a man of 30; a woman and a man of 46. The first
//! couple tries from month 1, conceives in month 5 and has the child in month 15; the
//! girl's series runs from month 1 with chance 0 until her 18th birthday (month 78), and
//! she dies of accident in month 83.9 without a child; the woman of 46 is past the window,
//! so her couple never tries.

